# Keep line endings identical everywhere, working tree included.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true has CRLF in the working tree while
# .editorconfig asks for LF, so `dotnet format --verify-no-changes` reports an ENDOFLINE error on
# almost every line of the repository. That noise is not merely annoying: it buries the real
# diagnostics, so a developer cannot use the formatter locally and only learns about an import
# ordering or whitespace problem when CI fails. CI runs on Linux, where the checkout is already LF,
# which is why the two disagreed.
#
# The committed content is already LF, so this changes no history -- only what lands on disk.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must not be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.snk binary
